    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 262,
        "text": "Welcome, everyone. Today we’re going to look at how historians interpret evidence. This is a simulated workshop, so please feel free to ask questions. Let’s start with this old letter. It was found in a box in the museum basement. What can we say about it?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "85149535819920e4b3d2fa1d119ba2b06585b4587f65063cea5d7cccf00b281b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 269,
        "sourceEnd": 390,
        "text": "Well, the paper looks old, and the handwriting is quite neat. It’s dated 1842. So it must be from the nineteenth century.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "4800a100a4fa2140bf9a42115595e30f3f188ac6f0aea124b4502cb1add53b4b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 398,
        "sourceEnd": 584,
        "text": "Good start. But we need to be careful. The date on the letter is 1842, but that doesn’t prove it was written then. Someone could have written it later and put an earlier date. What else?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "c22176bb13b9a787c092ff4e672dc7aa18dd3f1e024313b8ead1c0b22b0cd425",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 591,
        "sourceEnd": 731,
        "text": "The letter mentions a ship called the Mary Rose. It says the ship arrived in Liverpool on June 3rd. So maybe it’s a record of a real voyage.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "089f613df2cd33d3d761e5297e5a931613f36d6ead01665cb142b6ed79927a15",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 739,
        "sourceEnd": 836,
        "text": "Possibly. But we have to check other sources. Do we have any other documents about the Mary Rose?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "bfc4f7491126a8e3bb6a7ef853aa5e44dc9ba3fc8d509ad15dfea17f8e306aef",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 843,
        "sourceEnd": 963,
        "text": "I saw a newspaper from 1842 that mentions a ship with that name. But it says the ship arrived on June 5th, not June 3rd.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "95e8ebbb3469077a780fdb0c5e4952158df46b7d9e60fffda18e9b3cc58ff309",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 971,
        "sourceEnd": 1235,
        "text": "Interesting. So there’s a discrepancy. That doesn’t mean the letter is false; it might be that the letter was written by someone who remembered the date wrongly, or the newspaper made a mistake. Historians have to compare sources and decide which is more reliable.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "39fa1911934985b0d4103285a5ae80d70c752a21d5b8718c4bc208febcf3e43c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1242,
        "sourceEnd": 1282,
        "text": "So the letter isn’t completely reliable?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "9c5b4016c7282603005030e7f26e20195e813cfcc9ba6fc7710532b65625f7ea",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1290,
        "sourceEnd": 1502,
        "text": "It’s not about reliable or unreliable. It’s about understanding the context. For example, who wrote the letter? We don’t know. Why was it written? We don’t know that either. So we can’t be sure about its purpose.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "89511d9b537ec82f5cf95eeabb504da937389304c2f9b06e4a6cf714e27592ad",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1509,
        "sourceEnd": 1565,
        "text": "But we can still use it as evidence of something, right?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "b002b18fb47f340727f51d8344ac62913cfb3ab771ede87c962dd446117e552b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1573,
        "sourceEnd": 1762,
        "text": "Exactly. Even if it’s not accurate about the date, it can tell us about the language people used, or what kind of paper was available, or how people described ships. So it’s still valuable.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "fdb8b4dcf0d7426a70a18108aa5a5a7662bcf1b244111b4f338425c2d218ca3c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1769,
        "sourceEnd": 1829,
        "text": "I see. So we shouldn’t just accept everything at face value.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "0676afa335068e9f1a78f7eaaa41e40594f1eca28d4b98ab07f3d5d87b64ffc4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1837,
        "sourceEnd": 1954,
        "text": "Right. Now, let’s look at another example. This photograph shows a street scene from 1900. What can we learn from it?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "44f8f19c28121af37249c12cda67b50f3d48fd78d2715976cee3da0eec364c3b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1961,
        "sourceEnd": 2086,
        "text": "Well, there are horses and carriages, and people are wearing long dresses. So it’s definitely from before cars became common.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "7e015175325ef037966b1f16859811ad02f68c6bac8383d87cbded7edd24e031",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2094,
        "sourceEnd": 2363,
        "text": "Good observation. But be careful: the photo might have been taken later and show a historical reenactment. However, in this case, we have other evidence that it’s genuine. The photographer’s name is on the back, and we have a record of him working in that city in 1900.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "0c0934a12eb77ba1708e6f5d35b891ad2c3d87fbe24eabb1bb6dda45c388f729",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2370,
        "sourceEnd": 2430,
        "text": "So the photo is reliable because of the supporting evidence.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "eea4f1b4e29050088e3b3c5ee0832d44b62b91380ea74e6ffd32ccb67e5b7c2b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2438,
        "sourceEnd": 2570,
        "text": "Yes. That’s the key: we don’t judge a single source in isolation. We look at the whole picture. Now, let’s move on to the next item.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "fcdc233b53d6344064da2042dc349b9f2b5de65d4709f3830d07bd4e0f8fbce2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2577,
        "sourceEnd": 2598,
        "text": "What’s this? A diary?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "338c584a67acdf4ac296d0bd97b56e26370c20e93684a29972d7e087814773b4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2606,
        "sourceEnd": 2837,
        "text": "Yes, a diary from a soldier in 1916. It describes conditions in the trenches. But notice: the diary was published in 1920, after the war. So it might have been edited. We need to ask: is this the original diary, or a later version?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "02697a4f057a6e52bc1812e8a8656bee914834f95ffb05ce7e07465440f201d2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2844,
        "sourceEnd": 2910,
        "text": "The cover says “published 1920”, so it’s probably a later version.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "b6bdbfee8efbf42ef32b1f8eaf71c577714574150b96ff879137aaceb09b5fcb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2918,
        "sourceEnd": 3057,
        "text": "Exactly. So we can’t treat it as a direct, immediate record. It’s still useful, but we must consider the delay. Okay, any questions so far?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "71373ae3d6d0ca8d211674bfba17459e6f4dbb9307b2acdd55e13a2919167fc8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 3064,
        "sourceEnd": 3152,
        "text": "No, I think I understand. We need to ask who, when, why, and compare with other sources.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "9943fbf46c362870654edd7bc0d611312dd9f1621afd749283ea413b335fc45f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3160,
        "sourceEnd": 3257,
        "text": "Perfect summary. Let’s take a short break, and then we’ll practice with some documents ourselves.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "e6fa4ea39a5bef9070b81481887ac86270ffba4e0bbe2849f56e90cd9dd1f53b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
